Subject: [PATCH 9/9] [Spec Decode] Add a runtime speculation switch
 (set_speculation)

`collective_rpc("set_speculation", kwargs={"enabled": "0"|"1"})` switches
speculative decoding off and on at runtime without restarting the engine.
The switch has two halves kept in step by EngineCore.collective_rpc:
the scheduler stops scheduling speculative-token slots (so decoding is a
plain one token per step, instead of padded draft slots that would all be
rejected), and the GPU model runner stops proposing drafts (the drafter
and its weights stay loaded; the live tap keeps exporting the target's
committed tokens and aux hidden states). Switching back on takes effect
at the next scheduler step. Lets a controller apply the load-dependent
speculation frontier at runtime instead of a static per-batch-size table.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Tony Wen <jwen2914@uni.sydney.edu.au>
